 "summary": "No existing declaration in Mathlib or EpsilonEridani covers the standard orientation of EuclideanSpace, the light-front components, or the transverse boosts; Mathlib's only analogue is Complex.orientation/Complex.areaForm on \u2102 and there is no Module.Oriented instance for EuclideanSpace. The PR reuses Orientation.volumeForm_robust, areaForm_comp_linearIsometryEquiv, Matrix.det_fin_two and Physlib's minkowskiProduct_toCoord where applicable, and no near-clones exist in the repository.",
